^{:go/end 37} (go/func AppendFloat "AppendFloat appends src to dst as a JSON number per RFC 8259, section 6.\n\nExcept for -0, which is formatted as -0 instead of 0,\nthe output is identical to ECMA-262, 10th edition, section 7.1.12.1\nand (for 64-bit precision) identical to RFC 8785, section 3.2.2.3.\nThe values NaN, +Inf, and -Inf will be represented as a JSON string\nwith the values \"NaN\", \"Infinity\", and \"-Infinity\".\n\nNote that most JSON libraries and standards assume that JSON numbers\nare 64-bit floating-point numbers. As such, prefer using 64 bits\nof precision unless the recipient can know from other context\nthat the encoded number uses 32 bits of precision.\n" ^{:tag (slice byte)} [^{:tag (slice byte)} dst ^float64 src ^int bits]
  (when (and (!= bits 32) (!= bits 64))
    (panic "illegal AppendFloat bit size"))

  (jsonwire/AppendFloat dst src bits))








